[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Setup and authentication
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirement

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
First-run setup, web sessions, device tokens and secrets. UIDs: REQ-BE-010 .. 019.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-010
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: First-run setup
STATEMENT: >>>
While no user with a login exists, the web admin shall offer a setup wizard that creates the first administrator. Once a login user exists, the setup pages shall redirect to the login page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A fresh installation ships without accounts or default passwords.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-011
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Web sessions
STATEMENT: >>>
Web admin pages shall require a logged-in session (cookie ``buddyplan_session``); administrator pages shall additionally require administrator rights.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-012
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: API tokens per device
STATEMENT: >>>
``POST /api/auth/login`` shall exchange a valid username and password plus a device ID for a bearer token. Logging in again from the same device shall replace that device's token. Tokens shall be stored only as a peppered hash.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-013
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Device revocation
STATEMENT: >>>
A user shall be able to list and revoke their own logged-in devices, and an administrator those of any user. Requests with a revoked token shall get HTTP 401.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-014
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Required secrets
STATEMENT: >>>
The backend shall refuse to start without ``SESSION_SECRET_KEY`` and ``TOKEN_PEPPER``, unless ``BUDDYPLAN_DEV=1`` is set.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Prevents running production with guessable or missing secrets.
<<<
